# MAJORANA — Hyperdimensional Map Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph IDENT["Identity & Discrete Structure"]
    C["crystal_id"]
    L["15,625 lattice point IDs"]
    G["231 gate IDs"]
    SG["230 space-group IDs"]
    M["21×11 = 231 cells"]
  end
  subgraph SPACES["Independent Coordinate Spaces"]
    P3["Physical XYZ"]
    O4["Operational XYZW"]
    H126["Proposed 126D Hyper-Space"]
    S["Semantic Relation Graph"]
  end
  subgraph PROJECTIONS["Versioned Projection Layer"]
    PR1["2D / Mermaid topology"]
    PR2["3D spatial projection"]
    PR3["4D operational view"]
    PR4["Hyper-map / numerical projection"]
  end
  C --> L
  C --> G
  C --> SG
  G <-->|"explicit mapping only"| M
  L --> H126
  G --> S
  SG --> S
  H126 --> PR2
  H126 --> PR3
  H126 --> PR4
  S --> PR1
  P3 --> PR2
  O4 --> PR3
```

Rules:
- 15,625 points, 126 dimensions, 231 gates, 230 groups and 21×11 cells are separate dimensions/identities.
- 81×81 remains an unresolved candidate projection.
- Every projection records source snapshot, transform, invertibility and loss profile.
- Mermaid represents graph/process structure; it is not the 126D geometric renderer.